{"episodes":{"184365":"A surface trough crossed the islands, resulting in an increase in shower and thunderstorm activity, when combined with local effects. Some localized flooding was reported with this event.","184775":"Sufficient moisture and lift resulted in scattered showers and thunderstorms, some of which produced strong wind gusts and damage.","184986":"These storms created gusty outflow winds in excess of 60 mph across Central Nevada.","185534":"As multiple low-amplitude upper waves (embedded within broad zonal flow) traversed the Southern Plains, two rounds of convection occurred across the forecast area on the 19th. The first round, from the late morning into early afternoon, included a few reports of marginally severe hail across north-central into eastern Oklahoma, owing to relatively weak instability present during this time frame. ||By the early evening, aided by sufficient deep-layer wind shear and increasing (significant in magnitude) convective instability, multiple supercell thunderstorms initiated across southwest Oklahoma. Reports of large to very large hail and wind damage were received across the aforementioned areas. A 'left-split' (supercell) thunderstorm traveled into portions of central Oklahoma, including the southern suburbs of the Oklahoma City Metropolitan area, and produced continued reports of significant hail during the late evening time frame. Additional supercell thunderstorms developed further north across central Oklahoma during the evening as well. While a few reports of large hail were also received with these storms, greater convective inhibition limited the longevity of impact from these thunderstorms.","185535":"During the early evening of the 19th, aided by sufficient deep-layer wind shear and increasing (significant in magnitude) convective instability, multiple supercell thunderstorms initiated off of a dryline across western-north Texas. Reports of large to very large hail and wind damage were received across the area.","185536":"A small cluster of thunderstorms moved across portions of south-central Oklahoma during the early morning hours of the 20th. Despite strong convective inhibition in place, a report of wind damage occurred across central Garvin County, near the community of Elmore City.","185566":"Isolated severe storms produced damaging winds and large hail across portions of the Big Country and Concho Valley.","185576":"Afternoon sea breeze thunderstorms interacting with a weak stalled frontal boundary over central Florida produce gusty winds across Tampa Bay waters.","185743":"Thunderstorms pushing offshore produced strong wind gusts along the Brevard and Treasure Coasts.","185745":"A thunderstorm pushing offshore produced severe wind gusts along the southern Brevard County coast.","185788":"Scattered thunderstorms developed during the afternoon to early evening hours, moving over Greeley County. Storms were generally weak, with one producing pea to penny sized hail near the Greeley-Wallace County line.","185809":"An isolated severe thunderstorm moved slowly southward along the Montgomery-Labette county line near the Oklahoma-Kansas border. The storm produced quarter sized hail in far southeast Montgomery county before moving into Oklahoma.","185834":"Thunderstorms produced hail and winds across western Kansas.  A landspout was also reported.","186055":"An upper level disturbance passing by fueled spotty thunderstorms over the Mojave Desert. One produced flash flooding.","186119":"A large outflow boundary moved south southwest off mainland South Florida and across the Florida Keys.  Scattered gale-force wind gusts accompanied the showers and thunderstorms as they moved into an environment characterized by east southeast lower tropospheric and moist flow.","186120":"A weak mesoscale convective vortex tracked across the Mid-South and intensified |as it moved across the Mississippi Delta region where instability values climbed to over 1000 J/kg. This system produced a severe storm with damaging winds in Shelby County.","186141":"On September 19th, a robust storm produced some hail and damaging winds in Denton County, moving into Dallas County. Later that evening, a cluster of storms developed to our west and northwest, producing some hail and damaging winds in our western counties. On September 21st, another cluster of storms skirted along the Red River producing large hail in Denton County and flash flooding in Grayson County."},"events":[{"begin":"2023-09-20T00:00Z","county":"Ford","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-20T00:00Z","endLat":37.65,"endLon":-100.18,"episode":185834,"id":1140671,"injuries":0,"lat":37.65,"location":"8.98 S Howell","lon":-100.18,"magnitude":2.0,"source":"Trained Spotter","state":"KS","type":"Hail","wfo":"DDC"},{"begin":"2023-09-20T00:01Z","county":"Hardeman","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-20T00:01Z","endLat":34.2543,"endLon":-99.5342,"episode":185535,"id":1139014,"injuries":0,"lat":34.2543,"location":"1.44 WSW Chillicothe","lon":-99.5342,"magnitude":0.88,"source":"Law Enforcement","state":"TX","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2023-09-20T00:03Z","county":"Jackson","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-20T00:03Z","endLat":34.4341,"endLon":-99.3395,"episode":185534,"id":1139093,"injuries":0,"lat":34.4341,"location":"3.23 S Elmer","lon":-99.3395,"magnitude":1.0,"narrative":"MPing report.","source":"Public","state":"OK","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2023-09-20T00:08Z","county":"Kiowa","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-20T00:08Z","endLat":34.8601,"endLon":-99.0252,"episode":185534,"id":1139095,"injuries":0,"lat":34.8601,"location":"0.76 NNW Roosevelt","lon":-99.0252,"magnitude":2.0,"source":"Trained Spotter","state":"OK","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2023-09-20T00:08Z","county":"Kiowa","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-20T00:08Z","endLat":34.8053,"endLon":-98.9886,"episode":185534,"id":1139096,"injuries":0,"lat":34.8053,"location":"0.74 ENE Cold Springs","lon":-98.9886,"magnitude":1.75,"sour